      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: There is always a race here and only one small value picked up. There is an inherent latency inefficiency (magnified even more by preempt_disable()) here that could be dealt with by either using an atomic for cmdline_num to ensure corrupted value, or by acquiring cmdline_num into an unsigned local variable inside a lock, then run the scnprintf outside the lock.\n\nChanging to atomic could be too costly and too much impact if all accesses to cmdline_num are through atomic operations, so I would opt grabbing the value within the lock, and snprintf outside.\n\nscnprintf takes almost as long as a system call to format a string at times, time not well spent with preemption disabled ...",
